:HELP NAME=ADDRDBDIRE.Add RDB Directory Entry (ADDRDBDIRE)
:P.Use the Add RDB Directory Entry (ADDRDBDIRE) command to add an entry
to the relational database directory, kept in the data area
QUSRSYS/QRWRDBDIR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/RDB'.Entry (RDB)
:P.The entry for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relational database
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Relational database alias
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ARDPGM, *LOOPBACK, *MIRROR.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name or address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 254 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNA:EPK.
:PD.SNA.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/ARDPGM'.Application requester driver (ARDPGM)
:P.The application requester driver for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DRDA:EPK.
:PD.DRDA, the distributed relational database protocol.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Program
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/MODE'.Mode (MODE)
:P.The mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/TNSPGM'.Transaction program (TNSPGM)
:P.The transaction program for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DRDA:EPK.
:PD.DRDA, the distributed relational database protocol.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/PORT'.Port number or service program (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DRDA:EPK.
:PD.DRDA, the distributed relational database protocol.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 14 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/RMTAUTMTH'.Remote authentication method (RMTAUTMTH)
:P.The remote authentication method for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Preferred method
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*KERBEROS:EPK.
:PD.Kerberos.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USRENCPWD, *USRID, *USRIDPWD, *ENCUSRPWD,
*ENCRYPTED.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Allow lower authentication
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALWLOWER, *NOALWLOWER.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/SECCNN'.Secure connection (SECCNN)
:P.Whether the connection is secured with TLS.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SSL, *TLS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRDBDIRE/ENCALG'.Encryption algorithm (ENCALG)
:P.The encryption algorithm for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DES, *AES.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGDDMTCPA.Change DDM TCP/IP Attributes (CHGDDMTCPA)
:P.Use the Change DDM TCP/IP Attributes (CHGDDMTCPA) command to change
the attributes of the DDM and DRDA server&colon. whether it starts with
TCP/IP and how clients must authenticate. The server reads them when it
starts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMTCPA/AUTOSTART'.Autostart server (AUTOSTART)
:P.The autostart server for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMTCPA/PWDRQD'.Lowest authentication method (PWDRQD)
:P.The lowest authentication method for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KERBEROS:EPK.
:PD.Kerberos.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USRID, *VLDONLY, *USRIDPWD, *USRENCPWD,
*ENCUSRPWD, *ENCRYPTED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMTCPA/ENCALG'.Lowest encryption algorithm (ENCALG)
:P.The lowest encryption algorithm for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DES, *AES.
:EHELP.
