:HELP NAME=RMVRDBDIRE.Remove RDB Directory Entry (RMVRDBDIRE)
:P.Use the Remove RDB Directory Entry (RMVRDBDIRE) command to remove
entries from the relational database directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVRDBDIRE/RDB'.Entry (RDB)
:P.The entry for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLRMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKRDBDIRE.Work with RDB Directory Entries (WRKRDBDIRE)
:P.Use the Work with RDB Directory Entries (WRKRDBDIRE) command to list
the relational database directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRDBDIRE/RDB'.Entry (RDB)
:P.The entry for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRDBDIRE/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
